From fd2530e7022d9ecb7f99cb0b8501b2183d29e5a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 20:04:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(entities): preserve Bedrock spatial updates

Bedrock move-entity-delta packets may omit unchanged axes. Merge only the
supplied coordinates for local corrections and remote actors so omitted
axes cannot become zero. Preserve the rule that ignores non-forced local
updates.

Protocol 2193 also sends MotionPredictionHints instead of ordinary actor
velocity updates when spatial optimizations are enabled. Translate its
runtime ID and motion through the same Java velocity writer, retain its
ground state, and discard updates for actors that no longer exist. The
Mojang 1.26.51 metadata archive establishes the field order and omission
of the tick carried by SetActorMotion. Registered-handler tests verify
the encoded Java packet, unsigned runtime IDs, ground transitions, and
removed actors without replacing their positions.
